{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The repeated probes reproduce the central hazard: the small decorated color-7 body advances every click and destroys the 7×7 color-8 square on contact. Clicking the small body freezes it; clicks can also reposition the large square in some contexts. That makes “square survives” a necessary invariant, while distance from the square to a ring is the first dense-progress candidate. I’m mapping the large square’s valid one-click destinations next, before testing either ring as a goal."}}
